From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darkyzhou <me@zqy.io>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 15:39:22 +0000
Subject: loong64: add LoongArch64 support

This patch carries the downstream Chromium changes needed to build Electron on LoongArch64, including build configuration, sandbox/syscall support, Crashpad, SwiftShader, XNNPACK, GPU blocklist, LSX baseline handling, and native LLVM builder integration.

The native LLVM path is used for LoongArch64 Electron release builds because Chromium's bundled clang is an x86_64 toolchain and is not usable as the main compiler on the LoongArch64 builder. Chromium-clang-only flags are kept on the bundled clang path, while the native builder LLVM uses its per-target compiler-rt runtime directory.

It can be removed once Chromium and Electron provide upstream LoongArch64 Linux support with matching third-party dependency coverage.

